-
-Fastener sizes (Brian, 2026-10-31):
-- **M3** is the default for ordinary joints (frames, decks, covers, part-to-part).
-- **M6** for weight-bearing joints (rack, brackets, shelves; see [[m6-bracket-hardware]]).
-- **M2 / M2.5** only where the device forces it (e.g. the screen's own standoffs, Pi 4 mounting holes).
-- Brian has M3 countersunk and M2.5 socket-head screws on hand.
-- Always heat-set inserts, never self-tapping ([[no-self-tapping]]).
-
-**Why:** small screws are fragile and add BOM types. SCR5-H used M2.5 frame and deck screws where M3 fits.
-**How to apply:** pick M3 unless the part is weight-bearing (M6) or the hole is fixed by the device. If unsure which, ask Brian.
-
-Heat-set inserts on hand (Brian, 2026-10-31; read as thread x length x OD):
-- M6 x 5 x 8: the 7.6 mm bore matches the rack posts (proven).
-- M3 x 3 x 5: 4.2 mm bore, 4 mm deep.
-- M2.5 x 4 x 3.5: 3.2 mm bore, 5 mm deep.
