+
+Any part work follows `.claude/skills/new-part/SKILL.md`, which holds the steps. Why its rules exist (all Brian, 2026-11-05):
+
+- **Draft until printing, measure first, fit report by ID:** the CM1000 took 6 prints before the modem was measured, and ER6-A to H each got a full release with no print logged.
+- **`tools/release_part.py`** replaces the per-part build scripts and the by-hand 3MF and viewer steps. Its ID check reads only the source and its hole scan is a heuristic, so still confirm IDs and bores in the viewer. Its MRT-F test 3MF opened with both parts in Bambu Studio.
+- **`lib/workshop.scad` + pinned BOSL2:** proven shapes drifted when copied between parts. Move a shape into the library when a second part needs it and check it in `tools/test_workshop_lib.py`. Post rails are not in the library yet.
+- **Design margin:** SG8-M6-F's M6 heads sat right beside the sleeve lip: they fit, "but we should strive to not be so close every time."
+- **OpenSCAD snapshot:** 26–276x faster on three real parts with near-identical meshes. Old per-part build scripts hardcode 2021.01, so check the path when copying one. `manifold3d` is installed for exact clearance checks.
+
+Related: [[keep-proven-fit-dims]], [[keep-requested-features]], [[check-3mf-loads]].
